Now that we know how to create arrays and slices, let's learn how to iterate over their elements using a loop!

The [b]range[/b] form of the [b]for[/b] loop allows you to iterate over a slice:[code format="go" codeId="3346"]a := make([]int, 5)
a[1] = 2
a[2] = 3
    
for i, v := range a {
  fmt.Println(i, v)
} [/code]
During each iteration of the loop, it returns two values: the index of the element and its value.

If you want only the values, you can skip the index using an underscore:[code format="go" codeId="3347"]for _, v := range a {
fmt.Println(v)
} [/code]
[note]You can use ranges for slices as well as arrays.[/note]

