The range can also be used to iterate over the characters of a string.

[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header][code format="go" codeId="3348"]x := "hello"
for _, c := range x {
  fmt.Println(c)
}[/code]
This program outputs [b]Unicode code points[/b] of the characters.
If you want to output the actual characters, you can use the [b]Printf[/b]() function:[code format="go" codeId="3349"]for _, c := range x {
  fmt.Printf("%c \n", c)
}  [/code]
[note]The [b]Printf[/b]() function is similar to the one in C, taking the format of the output as its argument. [b]%c[/b] in our case denotes a character, while [b]\n[/b] defines a new line.[/note]
